=== p2-windows · W7 · page:analytics/WeeklyDigest (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:analytics/WeeklyDigest   kind=page   web route=/weekly-digest
Web source  : web/src/features/analytics/pages/WeeklyDigestPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300), maui-windows workload installed — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage / SchemaDriftPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "WeeklyDigestPage.xaml +
  WeeklyDigestPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Analytics" is mapped onto these real conventions; the
  surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("WeeklyDigest").
- Route: the manifest route /weekly-digest had no native RouteDefinition yet, so one was added to
  TeslaSync.App.Core/Navigation/RouteTable.cs — Page("WeeklyDigest","weekly-digest",RouteGroup.Analytics,
  "Weekly Digest","\uE787") — and the page factory was registered in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs
  (_viewModel.PageFactory.Register("WeeklyDigest", () => new FeatureViews.Analytics.WeeklyDigestPage())), next to
  the sibling W7 admin pages. This is the W4 NavigationView registration seam the prompt's allowed-files list calls
  out.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest extracted no API data source because the web page reads through the local
  useWeeklyDigest hook rather than a generated @/api hook. The native port reproduces that hook's full data flow
  through an injected IWeeklyDigestFeed: the default EmptyWeeklyDigestFeed resolves the empty state (matching the
  sibling-page host-injection precedent — the shell registers the parameterless ctor), and the generated-client
  WeeklyDigestClientFeed (WeeklyDigestPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI operations get_api_v1_vehicles
  (web useVehicles), get_api_v1_drives + get_api_v1_charging_sessions (with vehicle_id), and get_api_v1_alerts — the
  web /drives, /charging and /alerts reads — resolving the requested-or-first vehicle exactly like the web
  selectedVehicleId fallback. No HTTP touches the view; a failing fetch surfaces as the retriable error branch.
- SI cutover (ADR; frontend-si-cutover): the generated Drive/ChargingSession models are SI-canonical (Phase-48) —
  distance_m, duration_s, energy_used_wh, started_at/ended_at, total_energy_added_wh, start_soc_pct/end_soc_pct,
  cost_decimal. The projection reads SI off the wire and converts to the digest's display units (km, min, kWh,
  Wh/km, kW) at the display boundary only (WeeklyDigestProjection.Aggregate), never storing/computing non-SI — the
  presentational sections then render those values verbatim with their hard-coded unit suffixes, matching the web.
- The web page renders all four branches inside the PageContainer body. The native port reproduces them as visible
  Fluent regions per ADR-006: loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton shimmer stack (web DigestSkeleton); error -> TsQueryError
  (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry (web PageContainer error); empty -> TsGlassPanel + TsEmptyState with the Calendar
  glyph (web EmptyState); ready -> the FadeIn digest: an inline WeekSelector (prev/next TsButton + week label +
  Current TsBadge), an inline SummaryHeroCards grid of HighlightCard components, and the pre-built DrivingSection,
  ChargingSection, BatteryHealthSection, AlertsSection and the self-driving WeekOverWeekSummary (fed the page's
  already-computed metrics through a StaticWeekOverWeekSource). Never a blank region.
- The two web sub-components with no standalone native feature-view (WeekSelector, SummaryHeroCards) are reproduced
  inline as page-internal composition; the five sections that already exist as W3 feature-views are composed and
  fed render-ready models built by the projection. The web AIDigestNarration is a withAiFeature(...) no-op when
  ai_mode='off' (its own AI-feature unit) and is out of this page-shell unit's scope.
- All five manifest i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the exact web key names. Four
  (analytics.weeklyDigest.title / .subtitle / .selectVehicle / .noData) were already present in
  Strings/en/Resources.resw (added by the WeeklyDigest string-group + sibling section units); the fifth,
  analytics.weeklyDigest.noDataMessage, was added (plus analytics.weeklyDigest.funFactDesc for the inline hero fun
  fact). The ar/he catalogs lag en by design; the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=8

# Data states (3) — loading / empty / error, each a visible region (never blank)
[x] state  - loading  -> WeeklyDigestState.Loading + WeeklyDigestDisplay.ShowLoading; rendered
             WeeklyDigestPage.cs#_loadingSkeleton (the TsStatGridSkeleton shimmer stack, web DigestSkeleton); gated by
             WeeklyDigestProjection.Project (model.Loading precedence); tests State_loading_when_query_in_flight,
             Loading_precedence_beats_error_and_empty
[x] state  - empty    -> WeeklyDigestState.Empty + ShowEmpty; rendered WeeklyDigestPage.cs#_emptyPanel
             (TsGlassPanel + TsEmptyState, Calendar glyph + noData title + noDataMessage), web EmptyState; gated by
             !hasData (weekDrives.Count==0 && weekCharging.Count==0); tests State_empty_when_resolved_with_no_activity,
             Week_filtering_excludes_other_weeks, ViewModel_empty_feed_is_the_empty_state
[x] state  - error    -> WeeklyDigestState.Error + ShowError; rendered WeeklyDigestPage.cs#_errorState
             (TsQueryError + Retry via ActionInvoked -> RefreshAsync), web PageContainer error; gated by
             model.HasError; tests State_error_when_query_failed_shows_retry, ViewModel_feed_failure_is_the_error_state

# Strings (5) — every visible literal resolves from Strings/*.resw via ILocalizer with the web key names
[x] string - analytics.weeklyDigest.noData        -> WeeklyDigestProjection.Project localizer.GetString("analytics.weeklyDigest.noData", "No Data") -> EmptyTitle
[x] string - analytics.weeklyDigest.noDataMessage -> WeeklyDigestProjection.Project localizer.GetString("analytics.weeklyDigest.noDataMessage", "No driving or charging data found for this week.") -> EmptyMessage
[x] string - analytics.weeklyDigest.selectVehicle -> WeeklyDigestProjection.Project localizer.GetString("analytics.weeklyDigest.selectVehicle", "Select vehicle") -> SelectVehicleHint
[x] string - analytics.weeklyDigest.subtitle      -> WeeklyDigestProjection.Project localizer.GetString("analytics.weeklyDigest.subtitle", "Your driving and charging summary for the week") -> Subtitle
[x] string - analytics.weeklyDigest.title         -> WeeklyDigestProjection.Project / WeeklyDigestRegistration.Title localizer.GetString("analytics.weeklyDigest.title", "Weekly Digest") -> Title

